WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Your virtual machines. Browse guest states, configured resources and total allocated memory.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Create a guest. Choose a name, resources, owner setup and SSH. This example was cancelled.

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Guest Home. Inspect launch readiness and experimental suspend capability. Both guests stayed stopped.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Resources and factory. Inspect CPU, memory, disk capacity and the guest's recorded factory image.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Configure a stopped guest. Edit resources, clipboard and immersive mode while stopped. This form was cancelled.

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Networking. Each SSH-enabled guest has a distinct localhost port. Networking uses NAT.

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Startup and display. Choose windowed or immersive mode. Opening the manager does not start guests.

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
SSH from this Mac. A stopped guest is available on next launch. Copy SSH Command appears after verification.

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Mission Control Spaces. Use the running guest's Dock icon: Options, Assign To, This Desktop.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Import a prepared factory. Choose a reviewed compatible bundle. This form was cancelled without an import.

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Super shortcuts. Enable the manager in Accessibility yourself before starting guests.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Runtime and troubleshooting. Check host readiness and the known graphics startup limitation.
